.TH "RAPTOR-HISTORY" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-history \- list, snapshot or restore saved versions of a model
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor history\fR [\-h] [\-\-snapshot] [\-\-restore SNAPSHOT] [\-o PATH] [\-\-force] [\-f {text,json}] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Version history kept by the desktop application on save. Snapshots live in the user's private state folder, not beside the model.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshot\fR
record the file as it is now
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\fR \fISNAPSHOT\fR
write this snapshot to \-\-output (or \-\-force over MODEL)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR
destination for \-\-restore
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
allow \-\-restore to overwrite MODEL
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
